 026/04/Green-Tree-Frog-on-leaf.jpg
UID:ftoHglCW1YB98PJD-OGJp
SUMMARY:Froggy Night
DTSTAMP:20260713T123630Z
DTSTART:20260815T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:$37 member / $52 nonmemberInstructor: Dr. Cassidy Johnson Ages 
	21+ \n\n\n\nHop on over for a wet\, wild night! Enjoy refreshments (frog-t
	hemed snacks\, coffee\, and Saint Arnold Brewing Company beer) while you l
	earn all about the strange and wonderful world of frogs\, from their croak
	ing courtship to their mysterious metamorphosis. Weather permitting\, we’l
	l also go for a hike to search for frogs and other nocturnal creatures. \n
	\n\n\nPlease dress for the weather and wear walking shoes. \n\n\n\n\nregis
	ter online\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor bio: Dr. Cassidy Johnson has a B.S.
	 and M.S. in Biology at Texas A&M University – Corpus Christi and a Ph.D. 
	in Biochemistry & Cell Biology from Rice University. She loves teaching bi
	ology and is currently an Assistant Teaching Professor for Rice BioScience
	s. She fell in love with local amphibians while working for the Houston to
	ad ex situ conservation program at the Houston Zoo. She is also passionate
	 about the protection and restoration of Texas prairies and is on the boar
	d of the Native Prairie Association of Texas and was previously the presid
	ent of the Coastal Prairie Partnership.\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/ev
	ent/froggy-night/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/froggy-night/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Docent-Volunteer.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 024/04/Docent-Volunteer.jpg
UID:2iZiF9DzMNcuNs4jlY3ZE
SUMMARY:Docent Recruitment Open House & Breakfast
DTSTAMP:20260713T123630Z
DTSTART:20260820T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:FreeRegistration encouraged\; walk-in participants welcomeAges 
	21+ \n\n\n\nCalling all nature lovers! We are looking to grow our team of 
	Arboretum Docents and would like to invite you to learn more at this infor
	mational breakfast. Docents are volunteers who are specially trained to en
	gage visitors of all ages and backgrounds in active explorations of our tr
	ails and Discovery Room. We are currently recruiting individuals for our u
	pcoming docent trainings to prepare for fall programs! \n\n\n\n\nRSVP Onli
	ne\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nConcerned that you know very little about natural hist
	ory\, native flora/fauna\, or the Arboretum in general? Not to worry! Doce
	nt training is comprehensive and includes extensive content-based classes 
	as well as training on effective touring techniques. \n\n\n\nIf you are in
	terested in helping us teach our visitors about nature and all it has to o
	ffer\, we encourage you to attend!\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/d
	ocent-recruitment-open-house-breakfast/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature
	 Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/docent-recruitment-open-house-breakf
	ast/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonarboretum.or
 g/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Phenology-1280-x-720.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Phenology-1280-x-720.png
UID:H5eAIpOmoqEquQvd7V8AJ
SUMMARY:Fourth Saturday Phenology Walk
DTSTAMP:20260713T123630Z
DTSTART:20260822T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:Fourth Saturday of the Month9:00 – 11:00 amFree\, donations app
	reciatedAll ages\, minors must be accompanied by an adult \n\n\n\nMeet in 
	front of the Nature Center building \n\n\n\nDiscover the hidden seasonal r
	hythms of nature firsthand on our guided Phenology Walks\, where we track 
	the life cycles of different plants across ecosystems\, from the first spr
	ing bud burst to winter dormancy. You’ll learn how shifting weather patter
	ns and climate change influence the timing of these important events in ou
	r local ecosystems and how you can become a community scientist\, contribu
	ting vital data from your own backyard to a global research initiative.  \
	n\n\n\nThese relaxing morning walks are led by scientists from Rice Univer
	sity and staff from the Arboretum. We welcome nature enthusiasts of all ag
	es\, however kids 12 years and younger must be accompanied by a guardian. 
	\n\n\n\nLearn more about the study of phenology and ways you can contribut
	e at https://www.usanpn.org/nn \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCommunity Science Partner\n
	\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/fourth-saturday-phenology-walk/2026-0
	8-22/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/fourth-saturday-phenology-walk/2026-
	08-22/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
